keywords:
  - "modularity"
  - "information hiding"
  - "separation of concerns"
  - "boundary objects"
  - "namespace collision"
  - "declarative registry"
  - "reproducible review"
  - "open science"
abstract: >-
  A thin reader that declares what a set of small evaluative instruments
  is, reads whichever sibling packages are installed, and checks one
  narrow property: whether published enum member names collide without
  a matching declaration. It adds no instrument of its own and computes no
  aggregate; a legible reading says only that no unexempted published-name
  collision was found.
